# Version

The guide shows the version from `const VERSION` in `index.html`. The label is `versionLabel` (`版本` / `Version`). The number itself is not translated.

Before committing a user-visible change, raise `VERSION` and add the same notes in both places:

- the `CHANGELOG` array in `index.html` (Chinese and English)
- `CHANGELOG.md`

Small fixes and polish bump the patch number. Softening an animation that already exists is a patch: `1.2` becomes `1.2.1`.

A new capability bumps the middle number and drops the patch. `1.2.1` becomes `1.3`. `1.9` becomes `2.0`.

Judge from what the reader can now do. Do not raise the middle number for a correction.

Update the fallback text in `#app-version` to the same number. Do not add a second copy of the number in the language strings.
